      "text": "# Smart Complaint Routing \u0026 Workflow Automation System\n**Project Blueprint \u0026 System Specification**\n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary \u0026 Product Description\n\n### 1.1 Product Overview\nThe **Smart Complaint Routing System** is an automated issue resolution platform designed for educational campuses, municipal offices, and institutional facilities. \n\nStandard grievance portals act as static digital forms requiring manual human triage, which causes significant operational bottlenecks, misdirected assignments, and missed service deadlines. This system replaces manual triage with a closed-loop automated workflow:\n\n1. **Intelligent Ingestion:** Converts unstructured natural language reports into structured, validated ticket data using AI.\n2. **Deterministic Dispatch:** Assigns tickets to the optimal field team based on department mapping, worker availability, active workload, and location.\n3. **Automated SLA \u0026 Escalation Engine:** Tracks Service Level Agreements (SLAs) in real time and automatically escalates neglected issues up the administrative hierarchy.\n\n```\n+------------------+      +-------------------+      +--------------------+      +--------------------+\n|  User Complaint  | ---\u003e |   AI Triage \u0026     | ---\u003e | Smart Dispatch \u0026   | ---\u003e |  SLA Monitoring \u0026  |\n|  (Natural Text)  |      | Schema Validation |      | Workload Balancing |      | Auto-Escalation    |\n+------------------+      +-------------------+      +--------------------+      +--------------------+\n```\n\n### 1.2 Core Value Proposition\n* **Zero-Touch Triage:** Eliminates the manual administrative step of reading, categorizing, and assigning complaints.\n* **Accountability via SLAs:** Ensures every ticket has a strictly enforced resolution timeline based on its severity.\n* **Balanced Workload:** Prevents individual maintenance teams from being overloaded by dynamically scoring availability and active ticket counts.\n* **End-to-End Visibility:** Complainants receive transparent tracking, while administrators get real-time operational insights into bottlenecks and breaches.\n\n---\n\n## 2. End-to-End System Blueprint\n\n### 2.1 Operational Lifecycle\n```\n[User Submits Text / Image]\n            │\n            ▼\n[AI Extraction Layer (Gemini)]\n    - Category (e.g., Streetlight)\n    - Severity Indicators (e.g., Exposed wires)\n    - Location Target (e.g., Block C)\n            │\n            ▼\n[Backend Validation \u0026 Normalization]\n    - Maps category to authorized Department\n    - Applies deterministic priority rules (Low / Medium / High / Critical)\n            │\n            ▼\n[Dispatch Engine]\n    - Evaluates active workers in department\n    - Calculates Workload Score \u003d Active Tickets + Location Proximity\n    - Assigns ticket to best-scoring worker/team\n            │\n            ▼\n[Ticket Created with Dynamic SLA Deadline]\n    - e.g., High Priority \u003d 12-Hour Deadline\n            │\n            ▼\n[Background Scheduler Daemon]\n    ├─► If unresolved at (SLA - 2h)  ──\u003e Send Reminder Alert to Worker\n    ├─► If unresolved at Deadline    ──\u003e Escalate Ticket to Supervisor\n    └─► If unresolved at (SLA + 24h) ──\u003e Escalate to Department Head\n            │\n            ▼\n[Resolution \u0026 Closure]\n    - Worker marks resolved -\u003e Complainant confirms -\u003e Ticket Closed\n```\n\n### 2.2 Ticket State Machine\nTo ensure clean SLA tracking, tickets transition through strictly managed statuses:\n\n```\n[SUBMITTED] ──► [TRIAGED] ──► [ASSIGNED] ──► [IN_PROGRESS] ──► [RESOLVED] ──► [CLOSED]\n                                  │                │\n                                  └──[ESCALATED]◄──┘ (Triggered if SLA is breached)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Modular Team Work Breakdown\n\nTo allow multiple team members to work in parallel, the project is structured into **5 independent modules** with clear inputs and outputs.\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        MODULE 1: UI \u0026 DASHBOARDS                       │\n│       Complainant Portal   │   Worker Portal   │   Admin Dashboard     │\n└───────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                    │ REST / WebSockets\n┌───────────────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                     MODULE 5: DATABASE \u0026 API CORE                      │\n│        PostgreSQL Schemas  │  FastAPI Endpoints  │  Authentication     │\n└───────────────┬───────────────────┬───────────────────┬────────────────┘\n                │                   │                   │\n┌───────────────▼────────┐ ┌────────▼────────┐ ┌────────▼────────┐\n│       MODULE 2:        │ │       MODULE 3:        │ │       MODULE 4:        │\n│    AI TRIAGE ENGINE    │ │    DISPATCH ENGINE     │ │  SLA \u0026 ESCALATION CORE │\n│ LLM Parsing \u0026 Schema   │ │ Workload Scoring \u0026     │ │ Timers, Scheduler \u0026    │\n│ Validation Rules       │ │ Worker Assignment      │ │ Hierarchy Escalation   │\n└────────────────────────┘ └────────────────────────┘ └────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Module 1: Frontend \u0026 Role-Based Dashboards\n**Focus:** User Experience, Status Tracking, and Operational Views.\n\n* **Sub-module 1.1: Complainant Portal**\n  * Clean form interface (Title, Description, Campus Location dropdown/text, optional image upload).\n  * Public tracking page showing ticket progress bar (`Submitted` → `Assigned` → `In Progress` → `Resolved`).\n* **Sub-module 1.2: Maintenance Worker Portal**\n  * Task queue displaying assigned tickets sorted by SLA urgency.\n  * Quick-action buttons: `Acknowledge`, `Mark In-Progress`, `Resolve with Note`.\n* **Sub-module 1.3: Administrative Command Center**\n  * Real-time department metrics (Total Open, In Progress, Resolved).\n  * High-visibility **SLA Breach Alert Panel** showing escalated tickets requiring intervention.\n\n---\n\n### Module 2: Ingestion \u0026 AI Triage Pipeline\n**Focus:** Natural Language Processing and Deterministic Guardrails.\n\n* **Sub-module 2.1: Structured Extraction**\n  * Sends complaint text to Gemini using structured JSON output mode.\n  * Extracts: `inferred_category`, `extracted_location`, `hazard_flags`, `urgency_keywords`.\n* **Sub-module 2.2: Schema Validation \u0026 Normalization**\n  * Validates LLM output against an internal database mapping table (e.g., `water_leak` → `Plumbing Department`).\n  * If the LLM generates an unknown category, automatically assigns the ticket to `General Administration` for review.\n* **Sub-module 2.3: Priority Engine**\n  * Computes ticket priority deterministically using business rules rather than unconstrained AI decisions:\n    * **Critical (4h SLA):** Hazards (exposed wires, severe gas/water leaks, safety threats).\n    * **High (12h SLA):** Infrastructure breakdowns blocking daily routines (major outages).\n    * **Medium (24h SLA):** Standard failures (single streetlight, faulty tap).\n    * **Low (72h SLA):** Cosmetic/minor issues (faded signage, minor paint peeling).\n\n---\n\n### Module 3: Intelligent Dispatch Engine\n**Focus:** Assignment Optimization and Workload Balancing.\n\n* **Sub-module 3.1: Worker Registry \u0026 Availability**\n  * Maintains records of active workers, assigned departments, shifts, and designated campus zones.\n* **Sub-module 3.2: Assignment Scoring Algorithm**\n  * When a validated ticket arrives, the engine queries active workers in the target department and calculates an assignment score:\n  $$\\text{Score} \u003d (W_1 \\times \\text{Active Ticket Count}) + (W_2 \\times \\text{Location Distance Penalty})$$\n  * Assigns the ticket to the worker with the lowest score (least burdened, closest proximity).\n* **Sub-module 3.3: Manual Override Support**\n  * Allows administrators to reassign tickets manually without breaking the audit log.\n\n---\n\n### Module 