      "text": "# Version 1.0: The Functional Core — Module Breakdown\n\n---\n\n## 1. Execution Order \u0026 Parallel Work Overview\n\nTo build Version 1.0 efficiently in a group without blocking each other, the work is split into **3 stages**:\n\n```\n[STAGE 1: Setup Foundations] ──► Can be done SIMULTANEOUSLY by Backend \u0026 Frontend leads\n  ├── Backend: B1 (Database Setup)\n  └── Frontend: F1 (Project Shell \u0026 Theme)\n          │\n          ▼\n[STAGE 2: Core Features] ─────► Can be done SIMULTANEOUSLY across up to 4 people\n  ├── Person A (Backend):  B2 (Ingestion API \u0026 Keyword Rules)\n  ├── Person B (Backend):  B3 (Status Update \u0026 Fetch API)\n  ├── Person C (Frontend): F2 (Submission Form) \u0026 F3 (Public Tracker)\n  └── Person D (Frontend): F4 (Basic Internal Ticket List)\n          │\n          ▼\n[STAGE 3: Integration] ───────► Whole team connects and tests the end-to-end flow\n  └── Joint Task: I1 (API Wiring \u0026 End-to-End Verification)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Backend Modules (In Order of Execution)\n\n### **Module B1: Database Schema \u0026 Storage Setup**\n* **When to do:** **First** (Required before any other backend work).\n* **Can work simultaneously with:** Frontend Module F1.\n* **What it does:**\n  * Creates the database tables for **Departments** (e.g., Electrical, Plumbing, IT).\n  * Creates the core **Tickets** table (Fields: Ticket ID, Title, Description, Location, Department, Priority, Status, Created Timestamp, Updated Timestamp).\n  * Sets allowed statuses: `SUBMITTED`, `IN_PROGRESS`, `RESOLVED`.\n  * Seeds the database with default departments.\n\n---\n\n### **Module B2: Ticket Ingestion \u0026 Keyword Routing Engine**\n* **When to do:** After Module B1 is complete.\n* **Can work simultaneously with:** Module B3 and Frontend Modules F2 / F3.\n* **What it does:**\n  * Implements the `POST /tickets` API endpoint to accept complaint data.\n  * Runs a simple keyword-matching rule to pick a department (e.g., *\"light\"* or *\"power\"* ➔ Electrical; *\"leak\"* or *\"tap\"* ➔ Plumbing).\n  * Defaults unmapped complaints to a `General Maintenance` department.\n  * Generates a unique tracking reference code for the user.\n\n---\n\n### **Module B3: Ticket Lookup \u0026 Status Management API**\n* **When to do:** After Module B1 is complete (can run at the exact same time as B2).\n* **Can work simultaneously with:** Module B2 and Frontend Module F4.\n* **What it does:**\n  * Implements `GET /tickets/{id}` to fetch live ticket details for the tracking page.\n  * Implements `GET /tickets` to fetch all open tickets grouped by department for staff.\n  * Implements `PATCH /tickets/{id}/status` to change ticket state (`Submitted` ➔ `In Progress` ➔ `Resolved`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Frontend Modules (In Order of Execution)\n\n### **Module F1: Application Shell \u0026 Navigation Layout**\n* **When to do:** **First** (Required before building any specific frontend screens).\n* **Can work simultaneously with:** Backend Module B1.\n* **What it does:**\n  * Sets up the frontend project structure, base styling, and font configuration.\n  * Creates the global layout (Top header bar, clean page container, footer).\n  * Configures page routing for:\n    1. `/` (Complaint Submission Form)\n    2. `/track` (Public Status Tracker)\n    3. `/admin` (Basic Internal Ticket List)\n\n---\n\n### **Module F2: Public Complaint Submission Form**\n* **When to do:** After Module F1 is complete.\n* **Can work simultaneously with:** Frontend Modules F3 / F4 and Backend Module B2.\n* **What it does:**\n  * Builds the form inputs: Title, Description, and Campus Location (dropdown or text).\n  * Includes basic client-side validation (ensures fields are not empty before submitting).\n  * Displays a **Success Modal** showing the generated Ticket ID upon submission with a \"Copy Tracking Code\" button.\n\n---\n\n### **Module F3: Public Ticket Status Tracking Screen**\n* **When to do:** After Module F1 is complete.\n* **Can work simultaneously with:** Frontend Modules F2 / F4 and Backend Module B3.\n* **What it does:**\n  * Builds a search box where users enter their Ticket Reference ID.\n  * Displays the ticket details card: Title, Description, Assigned Department, and Date Submitted.\n  * Shows a 3-step visual status bar indicating current progress (`Submitted` ➔ `In Progress` ➔ `Resolved`).\n\n---\n\n### **Module F4: Basic Internal Ticket List \u0026 Status Controller**\n* **When to do:** After Module F1 is complete.\n* **Can work simultaneously with:** Frontend Modules F2 / F3 and Backend Module B3.\n* **What it does:**\n  * Builds a basic staff/admin table listing all submitted tickets.\n  * Provides a simple dropdown/button on each row to change status (`Mark In Progress`, `Mark Resolved`).\n  * Includes a simple filter to view tickets by Department or Status.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Integration Stage (Final Joint Step)\n\n### **Module I1: End-to-End Wiring \u0026 Verification**\n* **When to do:** Once all B and F modules are built.\n* **Who works on it:** Backend and Frontend leads together.\n* **What it does:**\n  * Connects the Frontend forms and tables to the live Backend API endpoints.\n  * Verifies the complete end-to-end loop:\n    1. Submit complaint on web form ➔\n    2. Ticket saves to database with correct keyword department ➔\n    3. User tracks ticket using tracking code ➔\n    4. Staff updates status to `Resolved` in admin view ➔\n    5. User tracking screen reflects `Resolved`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Summary: Team Role Allocation (3 to 4 People)\n\n| Team Member | Assigned Tasks | Can Start Immediately? |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Member 1 (Backend Lead)** | Module B1 (Database), then Module B2 (Ingestion \u0026 Routing) | **Yes** (Starts on B1) |\n| **Member 2 (Backend / API)** | Module B3 (Lookup \u0026 Status APIs) | Starts right after B1 schema is defined |\n| **Member 3 (Frontend Lead)** | Module F1 (Layout Shell), then Module F2 (Submission Form) \u0026 F3 (Tracker) | **Yes** (Starts on F1) |\n| **Member 4 (Frontend UI)** | Module F4 (Admin Ticket List \u0026 Status Actions) | Starts right after F1 layout is ready |",
