      "text": "# Module B1: Database Schema \u0026 Storage Setup — Detailed Blueprint\n\n---\n\n## 1. Module Objective\nTo establish the foundational database structure that stores departments and complaint tickets. This schema is designed to be **future-proof**: it handles the simple ticketing needs of Version 1.0 while including placeholder columns so that future features (AI classification, smart dispatch, and SLA timers) can be added in later versions without rewriting or breaking the database.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Entity Specifications (Table Blueprints)\n\n### Entity 1: Departments (`departments`)\nThis table holds the master list of all service teams on campus.\n\n* **Department ID:** A unique numeric identifier (Primary Key, auto-incrementing).\n* **Department Name:** Short text label (e.g., \"Electrical\", \"Plumbing\", \"Sanitation\"). *Must be unique and mandatory.*\n* **Description:** Plain text summarizing what issues this department handles (e.g., \"Handles lights, wiring, power cuts, and appliances\"). *Mandatory.*\n* **Is Active:** A true/false flag to enable or disable departments without deleting them. *Defaults to True.*\n* **Created Timestamp:** Exact date and time the department was added to the system.\n\n---\n\n### Entity 2: Complaint Tickets (`tickets`)\nThis is the core table holding every complaint submitted to the platform.\n\n* **Internal Ticket ID:** A unique system identifier (UUID or standard primary key) used by internal database relationships.\n* **Public Tracking Code:** A short, human-readable reference code displayed to the user (e.g., `TICK-8492` or `CMP-1049`). *Must be unique and indexed for fast lookup.*\n* **Title:** A brief summary of the issue (Max 150 characters). *Mandatory.*\n* **Description:** The full plain-text explanation submitted by the user. *Mandatory.*\n* **Location Description:** The text or building name provided by the user (e.g., \"Hostel Block B, 2nd Floor\"). *Mandatory.*\n* **Department ID:** References the **Department ID** from the Departments table. *Mandatory (links every ticket to an authorized department).*\n* **Status:** Current progress of the ticket. *Restricted to 3 values in Version 1.0:*\n  * `SUBMITTED` *(Default state on creation)*\n  * `IN_PROGRESS`\n  * `RESOLVED`\n* **Priority Level:** Standard urgency rating. *Restricted to:* `LOW`, `MEDIUM`, `HIGH`, `CRITICAL`. *(Defaults to `MEDIUM` in Version 1.0).*\n* **Created Timestamp:** Exact date and time the ticket was submitted. *Automatically recorded.*\n* **Updated Timestamp:** Exact date and time of the last modification (e.g., status change). *Automatically updated.*\n* **Resolved Timestamp:** Date and time the ticket was marked as resolved. *Empty until status becomes `RESOLVED`.*\n\n---\n\n### Entity 3: Future-Proofing Placeholder Columns (Nullable for V1.0)\nTo ensure future versions do not require database migrations that wipe existing data, include these optional columns now:\n\n* **Assigned Worker ID:** Placeholder for Version 3.0 worker dispatch. *(Allowed to be empty/null in V1.0).*\n* **SLA Deadline Timestamp:** Placeholder for Version 4.0 timer tracking. *(Allowed to be empty/null in V1.0).*\n* **Resolution Notes:** Plain text entered by staff explaining what fix was performed. *(Allowed to be empty/null in V1.0).*\n\n---\n\n## 3. Initial Seed Data (Pre-Populated Records)\n\nAs part of completing Module B1, the database must be seeded with these **6 standard campus departments**:\n\n| Department ID | Department Name | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1** | **Electrical** | Handles power cuts, broken lights, fans, faulty switches, and wiring issues. |\n| **2** | **Plumbing** | Handles water leaks, broken taps, pipe bursts, clogged drains, and water shortage. |\n| **3** | **Sanitation \u0026 Housekeeping** | Handles garbage accumulation, dirty washrooms, cleaning requests, and pest control. |\n| **4** | **Civil Maintenance** | Handles broken doors, cracked walls, window glass damage, and furniture repairs. |\n| **5** | **IT \u0026 Network Support** | Handles campus Wi-Fi outages, ethernet port damage, and lab printer issues. |\n| **6** | **General Administration** | Fallback department for complaints that do not clearly fit standard categories. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Business \u0026 Validation Rules for Module B1\n\n1. **Strict Status Values:** The database must reject any status value other than `SUBMITTED`, `IN_PROGRESS`, and `RESOLVED`.\n2. **Mandatory Department Link:** A ticket cannot exist without being tied to a valid Department ID. If a complaint is unclassified, it must link to `General Administration` (ID: 6).\n3. **Automatic Tracking Code Generation:** Every new ticket must automatically receive a clean, uppercase alphanumeric tracking code (e.g., `TICK-` followed by numbers or letters) that users can easily copy.\n4. **Timezone Uniformity:** All timestamps (`created_at`, `updated_at`, `resolved_at`) must be stored in standardized Coordinated Universal Time (UTC).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Checklist for the Assigned Developer\n\n- [ ] Set up the local database instance.\n- [ ] Create the **Departments** table with unique constraints on the department name.\n- [ ] Create the **Tickets** table with foreign key reference to the Departments table.\n- [ ] Insert the 6 pre-populated seed departments into the database.\n- [ ] Add database indexes on `public_tracking_code`, `status`, and `department_id` to ensure instant lookup speeds.\n- [ ] Verify database rules by attempting test inserts:\n  - Verify a ticket successfully saves with default status `SUBMITTED`.\n  - Verify a ticket fails to save if an invalid department ID is provided.\n  - Verify a ticket fails to save if an unauthorized status string is provided.\n- [ ] Export database connection details and schema definitions to share with the developers working on Modules **B2** and **B3**.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Handoff Contract (What B2 and B3 Receive)\n\nOnce Module B1 is finished, developers on **B2 (Ingestion API)** and **B3 (Status API)** can rely on the following:\n\n* **For Module B2:** When creating a ticket, you must supply `title`, `description`, `location_description`, and `department_id`. The database will automatically assign the `tracking_code`, set status to `SUBMITTED`, priority to `MEDIUM`, and timestamp `created_at`.\n* **For Module B3:** You can query tickets directly by `public_tracking_code` or `department_id`, and update status strictly between `SUBMITTED`, `IN_PROGRESS`, and `RESOLVED`.",
