      "text": "# Module F2: Public Complaint Submission Form — Detailed Blueprint\n\n---\n\n## 1. Module Objective\nTo create the public-facing complaint submission interface hosted at the root route (`/`). \n\nThis module collects user grievance details, enforces client-side validation, submits the data to the **Ticket Ingestion API (Module B2)**, handles loading and error states, and presents a clear confirmation receipt modal containing the newly generated tracking code.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Visual Layout \u0026 Screen Architecture\n\nThe submission page is wrapped inside the global application shell created in **Module F1** and centers a structured form card on the screen:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                 SUBMIT A CAMPUS COMPLAINT                   │\n│   Report facility issues for quick automated resolution.    │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                             │\n│  Complaint Title *                                          │\n│  [ e.g., Water leakage in 2nd floor bathroom             ]  │\n│  (Small helper text: Keep it short and specific)            │\n│                                                             │\n│  Campus Location *                                          │\n│  [ e.g., Hostel Block C, Room 204 or North Gate Library  ]  │\n│                                                             │\n│  Issue Description *                                        │\n│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n│  │ Describe the problem in detail...                     │  │\n│  │                                                       │  │\n│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n│  Character count: 0 / 2000                                  │\n│                                                             │\n│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n│  │               [ Submit Complaint Button ]             │  │\n│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Field Specifications \u0026 Client-Side Validation\n\nThe form contains three primary input fields. To prevent unnecessary network calls, all fields must be validated in the browser before triggering the backend API.\n\n### 3.1 Field 1: Complaint Title\n* **Input Type:** Single-line text input.\n* **Placeholder:** *\"e.g., Streetlight not working outside Block C\"*\n* **Validation Rules:**\n  * Mandatory field.\n  * Minimum length: **5 characters**.\n  * Maximum length: **150 characters**.\n* **Inline Error Triggers:**\n  * *\"Title is required.\"* (If left blank on submit)\n  * *\"Title must be at least 5 characters.\"* (If too short)\n\n---\n\n### 3.2 Field 2: Campus Location\n* **Input Type:** Single-line text input with standard campus location suggestions.\n* **Placeholder:** *\"e.g., Hostel Block B - 3rd Floor Washroom\"*\n* **Validation Rules:**\n  * Mandatory field.\n  * Minimum length: **3 characters**.\n  * Maximum length: **100 characters**.\n* **Inline Error Triggers:**\n  * *\"Location is required so maintenance teams know where to go.\"*\n\n---\n\n### 3.3 Field 3: Issue Description\n* **Input Type:** Multi-line text area (4 to 6 rows tall).\n* **Placeholder:** *\"Provide specific details about the issue (e.g., how long it has been happening, exact room number, any safety concerns)...\"*\n* **Live Features:**\n  * A live character counter in the bottom-right corner displaying `Current Characters / 2000`.\n* **Validation Rules:**\n  * Mandatory field.\n  * Minimum length: **10 characters**.\n  * Maximum length: **2,000 characters**.\n* **Inline Error Triggers:**\n  * *\"Description must be at least 10 characters so we can understand the problem.\"*\n  * *\"Description cannot exceed 2,000 characters.\"*\n\n---\n\n## 4. Interactive Form States \u0026 Lifecycle\n\nThe form transitions through five distinct visual states during user interaction:\n\n```\n[1. Idle State] ──────► [2. Validating State] ───► [3. Submitting State]\n  (Clean inputs)           (Checking fields)         (Button shows spinner)\n                                  │                            │\n                                  ▼                            ├──► [4. API Error Banner]\n                           (Errors shown under fields)         │      (Server down / retry)\n                                                               │\n                                                               └──► [5. Success Modal]\n                                                                      (Shows Tracking Code)\n```\n\n1. **Idle State:** The default empty form with clear placeholders and active inputs.\n2. **Field Error State:** If the user clicks \"Submit\" with invalid data, the border of invalid fields turns red, and clear error text appears directly below the offending input.\n3. **Submitting / Loading State:**\n   * The submit button text swaps to a spinning loader and reads *\"Submitting issue...\"*.\n   * All form fields and the button are temporarily disabled to prevent accidental double-clicks.\n4. **API Error State:**\n   * If the backend is unreachable or returns a server error, a prominent red alert banner drops down at the top of the form stating: *\"Unable to submit ticket. Please check your network and try again.\"*\n   * Form inputs remain intact so the user does not lose their typed text.\n5. **Success State:** Opens the **Confirmation Receipt Modal**.\n\n---\n\n## 5. The Success Receipt \u0026 Confirmation Modal\n\nWhen Module B2 successfully returns a response, the form dims and a prominent, centered modal popup appears:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    ✓ COMPLAINT SUBMITTED                    │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                             │\n│  Your Tracking Reference Code:                              │\n│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n│  │                      TICK-8492                        │  │\n│  │               [ 📋 Copy Code Button ]                 │  │\n│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n│                                                             │\n│  • Assigned Department:  Plumbing                           │\n│  • Initial Status:       Submitted (Pending Review)         │\n│  • Submitted At:         Just now                           │\n│                                                             │\n│  Please save your tracking code to monitor progress.        │\n│                                                             │\n│  [ Track This Complaint ]        [ Submit Another Issue ]   │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### 5.1 Success Modal Elements\n* **Large Tracking Code Box:** Displays the generated reference code (e.g., `TICK-8492`) in bold, prominent text.\n* **1-Click Copy Button:** Copies the code to the user\u0027s clipboard and temporarily changes to a green checkmark reading *\"Copied!\"*.\n* **Assigned Department Pill:** Displays the automatically assigned department name returned by the routing engine.\n* **Action Button 1: *\"Track This Complaint\"*:** Directs the user immediately to `/track` with their tracking code pre-filled.\n* **Action Button 2: *\"Submit Another Issue\"*:** Closes the modal, clears all form fields, and resets the form to its clean state.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Implementation Checklist for the Assigned Developer\n\n- [ ] Place the main form component inside the `/` route shell established in Module F1.\n- [ ] Build the form layout using the shared `Card`, `Input`, `Textarea`, and `Button` primitives.\n- [ ] Connect the live character counter to the description text area.\n- [ ] Implement client-side validation logic checking min/max constraints before triggering the API.\n- [ ] Wire up the `POST /api/tickets` API request to send `title`, `description`, and `location_description`.\n- [ ] Implement loading spinner and button-disable logic during active network requests.\n- [ ] Build the **Success Modal** overlay:\n  - [ ] Render the returned `public_tracking_code` and `assigned_department`.\n  - [ ] Implement the \"Copy to Clipboard\" button with visual confirmation feedback.\n  - [ ] Implement the \"Track This Complaint\" navigation link redirecting to `/track`.\n  - [ ] Implement the \"Submit Another Issue\" form reset button.\n- [ ] Verify error handling by testing the form when the backend server is intentionally stopped.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Handoff Contract (What Connects to F3)\n\n* When the user clicks **\"Track This Complaint\"** in the success modal, Module F2 passes the generated tracking code as a URL parameter to the tracking screen (e.g., `/track?code\u003dTICK-8492`).\n* **Module F3 (Tracking Screen)** will automatically read this code and fetch the ticket status immediately without making the user re-type it.",
