      "text": "# Module F3: Public Ticket Status Tracking Screen — Detailed Blueprint\n\n---\n\n## 1. Module Objective\nTo create the public-facing status tracking interface hosted at the `/track` route. \n\nThis module allows complainants to enter their tracking code (e.g., `TICK-8492`), queries the **Ticket Lookup API (Module B3)**, and renders an interactive status card featuring a visual 3-step progress bar and detailed ticket information.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Visual Layout \u0026 Screen Architecture\n\nThe tracking page consists of two visual sections: the **Tracking Search Bar** at the top and the **Ticket Details \u0026 Progress Card** below.\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    TRACK YOUR COMPLAINT                     │\n│    Enter your tracking reference code to check progress.    │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                             │\n│  Tracking Reference Code                                    │\n│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐ ┌───────────────┐ │\n│  │ e.g., TICK-8492                      │ │ [ Track ]     │ │\n│  └──────────────────────────────────────┘ └───────────────┘ │\n│                                                             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n                  (Appears after search)\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [ TICK-8492 ]   Water leakage in 2nd floor bathroom        │\n│  Department: Plumbing  •  Priority: Medium  •  [ 🔄 Refresh]│\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                             │\n│                    3-STAGE PROGRESS BAR                     │\n│                                                             │\n│      (✓) ───────────────── (●) ───────────────── (○)        │\n│   Submitted            In Progress            Resolved      │\n│   Oct 24, 10:30 AM     Oct 24, 02:15 PM       Pending       │\n│                                                             │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  TICKET DETAILS                                             │\n│                                                             │\n│  • Location:      Hostel Block C, Room 204                  │\n│  • Submitted On:  October 24, 2026 at 10:30 AM             │\n│  • Last Update:   October 24, 2026 at 02:15 PM              │\n│                                                             │\n│  Original Description:                                      │\n│  \"The pipe under the second sink has burst and is flooding  │\n│  the corridor.\"                                             │\n│                                                             │\n│  Resolution Notes:                                          │\n│  (Empty while in progress / Shows staff fix details once done)\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. The 3-Stage Visual Progress Bar\n\nThe core of the tracking page is a horizontal visual progress bar showing the lifecycle of the complaint:\n\n```\n[Step 1: Submitted] ──────► [Step 2: In Progress] ──────► [Step 3: Resolved]\n```\n\n### 3.1 Visual Rules for Each Step\n* **Completed Step:**\n  * Displays a solid green circular icon with a checkmark (`✓`).\n  * The connecting line leading to the next step turns solid green.\n  * Displays the timestamp when this milestone was reached.\n* **Active / Current Step:**\n  * Displays a bold, highlighted accent circle (`●`) with a subtle glowing pulse.\n  * Text is bold and clearly reads the current action (e.g., *\"Maintenance team is currently attending to this issue\"*).\n* **Future / Pending Step:**\n  * Displays a muted gray hollow circle (`○`).\n  * Connecting line remains a dim gray dotted or solid line.\n  * Subtext reads *\"Pending\"*.\n\n### 3.2 Status Mapping Logic\n* If Status is **`SUBMITTED`**:\n  * Step 1 (`Submitted`) is Active.\n  * Steps 2 and 3 are Pending.\n* If Status is **`IN_PROGRESS`**:\n  * Step 1 (`Submitted`) is Complete (`✓`).\n  * Step 2 (`In Progress`) is Active (`●`).\n  * Step 3 (`Resolved`) is Pending (`○`).\n* If Status is **`RESOLVED`**:\n  * Step 1 (`Submitted`) is Complete (`✓`).\n  * Step 2 (`In Progress`) is Complete (`✓`).\n  * Step 3 (`Resolved`) is Complete (`✓`).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Screen Lifecycle \u0026 Interactive States\n\nThe tracking view handles four distinct UI states:\n\n```\n[1. Initial Empty State] ────► User clicks Track ────► [2. Loading Skeleton]\n  (Shows search bar +                                        │\n   search prompt)                                            ├──► [3. Not Found State]\n                                                             │      (Red error card)\n                                                             │\n                                                             └──► [4. Success State]\n                                                                    (Shows Progress Card)\n```\n\n1. **Initial Empty State:**\n   * Displays the search box and a friendly placeholder prompt: *\"Enter your tracking code above to check the status of your complaint.\"*\n2. **Loading State:**\n   * When the user clicks \"Track\", the button shows a spinner.\n   * A shimmering loading placeholder appears below the search bar to prevent sudden layout jumps.\n3. **Not Found / Error State:**\n   * If the tracking code does not exist in the database, a red-bordered alert box appears: *\"No complaint found matching code \u0027TICK-XXXX\u0027. Please double-check your code and try again.\"*\n4. **Success State:**\n   * Renders the complete **Ticket Details \u0026 Progress Card**.\n   * Includes a **\"Refresh Status\"** button so users can check for live updates without refreshing the entire web page.\n\n---\n\n## 5. URL Parameter Auto-Search (Seamless Bridge from F2)\n\nWhen a user submits a complaint on the submission form (**Module F2**) and clicks *\"Track This Complaint\"*, the application directs them to `/track?code\u003dTICK-8492`.\n\n* **Automatic Detection:** Upon page load, Module F3 checks if a `code` parameter exists in the URL.\n* **Auto-Fill \u0026 Execute:**\n  * If found, the tracking code is automatically inserted into the search input box.\n  * The system immediately fires the lookup query to the backend without requiring the user to click the \"Track\" button manually.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Implementation Checklist for the Assigned Developer\n\n- [ ] Place the tracking component inside the `/track` route established in Module F1.\n- [ ] Build the top search bar using the shared `Input` and `Button` primitives from F1.\n- [ ] Implement URL query parameter detection (read `?code\u003dXXXX` and auto-search on mount).\n- [ ] Wire up the `GET /api/tickets/{code}` API request to fetch ticket details from Module B3.\n- [ ] Build the **3-Stage Progress Bar Component**:\n  - [ ] Implement visual states (Completed green check, Active glowing circle, Pending gray circle).\n  - [ ] Implement timestamp display below each step milestone.\n- [ ] Build the **Ticket Details Grid**:\n  - [ ] Display Title, Assigned Department Pill, Location, Priority Pill, and Dates.\n  - [ ] Render the original full description.\n  - [ ] Conditionally render the Resolution Notes box if the ticket is `RESOLVED`.\n- [ ] Build the **\"Refresh Status\"** button allowing users to re-fetch the latest data on demand.\n- [ ] Build the **\"Not Found\"** error card for invalid tracking codes.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Handoff Contract (Integration Verification)\n\n* **With Module B3 (Backend API):** Module F3 sends the tracking code to `GET /api/tickets/{code}` and expects back: Title, Description, Location, Department Name, Status (`SUBMITTED`, `IN_PROGRESS`, `RESOLVED`), Created Timestamp, Updated Timestamp, and Resolution Notes (if any).\n* **With Module F2 (Frontend Submission):** Verifies that clicking \"Track\" on F2\u0027s confirmation modal lands on F3 with the search already completed and the progress bar visible.",
