      "text": "# Module B3: Ticket Lookup \u0026 Status Management API — Detailed Blueprint\n\n---\n\n## 1. Module Objective\nTo build the backend API endpoints responsible for reading ticket data and updating ticket progress. \n\nThis module serves two distinct audiences:\n1. **The Public Tracking Screen (Module F3):** Looks up a single ticket using its tracking reference code.\n2. **The Internal Staff Portal (Module F4):** Fetches filtered lists of all open tickets and allows maintenance staff to update ticket statuses (`Submitted` ➔ `In Progress` ➔ `Resolved`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. API Endpoint Specifications\n\nModule B3 exposes **three core endpoints**:\n\n```\n[Module B3: Read \u0026 Update Engine]\n    ├── 1. GET   /api/tickets/{code}          ──► Fetches single ticket for Public Tracker (F3)\n    ├── 2. GET   /api/tickets                 ──► Fetches all tickets with filters for Staff (F4)\n    └── 3. PATCH /api/tickets/{id}/status     ──► Updates ticket progress \u0026 records fix notes (F4)\n```\n\n---\n\n### Endpoint 1: Public Ticket Lookup by Code\n* **Action / HTTP Method:** `GET`\n* **Route Path:** `/api/tickets/{tracking_code}`\n* **Access Level:** Public\n\n#### What It Does:\n* Takes the alphanumeric tracking code from the URL (e.g., `TICK-8492`).\n* Performs a case-insensitive search against the database.\n* Merges the ticket record with its corresponding Department name.\n* Returns complete ticket details: Title, Description, Location, Department Name, Current Status, Priority, Date Submitted, Last Updated Date, and Resolution Notes (if already resolved).\n* If no matching code is found, returns a clean `404 Not Found` error.\n\n---\n\n### Endpoint 2: Staff Ticket Directory \u0026 Filtering\n* **Action / HTTP Method:** `GET`\n* **Route Path:** `/api/tickets`\n* **Access Level:** Internal / Staff (Open in V1.0)\n\n#### What It Does:\n* Retrieves a list of all tickets stored in the system, sorted with the newest complaints at the top.\n* Supports optional query filtering parameters:\n  * **Filter by Department:** (e.g., `/api/tickets?department_id\u003d2` to show only Plumbing complaints).\n  * **Filter by Status:** (e.g., `/api/tickets?status\u003dSUBMITTED` to show only unaddressed complaints).\n* Returns an array of ticket summary cards containing: Ticket ID, Tracking Code, Title, Location, Department Name, Status, Priority, and Submission Timestamp.\n\n---\n\n### Endpoint 3: Ticket Status \u0026 Resolution Update\n* **Action / HTTP Method:** `PATCH`\n* **Route Path:** `/api/tickets/{ticket_id}/status`\n* **Access Level:** Internal / Staff\n\n#### Expected Input Data:\n1. **New Status:** Must strictly be one of: `SUBMITTED`, `IN_PROGRESS`, or `RESOLVED`. *(Mandatory)*\n2. **Resolution Notes:** Plain text entered by the staff worker explaining what was done (e.g., *\"Replaced 40W tube light and tested switchboard\"*). *(Mandatory if status is set to `RESOLVED`; optional otherwise).*\n\n#### Business \u0026 Validation Rules:\n* **Strict State Transition:** Rejects invalid status strings immediately.\n* **Resolution Notes Enforcement:** The system must reject an update to `RESOLVED` if the staff worker leaves the resolution note blank.\n* **Automatic Timestamps:**\n  * Every status change automatically updates the `updated_at` timestamp to the current UTC time.\n  * Changing status to `RESOLVED` automatically stamps the `resolved_at` column with the current UTC time.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Transformation \u0026 Output Structure\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    API OUTPUT DEFINITIONS                   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                             │\n│  Single Ticket Output (Endpoint 1):                         │\n│  • Public Tracking Code:   \"TICK-8492\"                      │\n│  • Title:                  \"Water leakage in 2nd floor\"     │\n│  • Description:            \"Pipe burst under the sink...\"   │\n│  • Location:               \"Hostel Block C, Room 204\"       │\n│  • Department Name:        \"Plumbing\"                       │\n│  • Status:                 \"IN_PROGRESS\"                    │\n│  • Priority:               \"MEDIUM\"                         │\n│  • Created At:             \"2026-10-24T10:30:00Z\"           │\n│  • Updated At:             \"2026-10-24T14:15:00Z\"           │\n│  • Resolution Notes:       null / string                    │\n│                                                             │\n│  Ticket Directory Output (Endpoint 2):                      │\n│  • Total Tickets Count:    42                               │\n│  • Results Array:          [ {Ticket 1}, {Ticket 2}, ... ]  │\n│                                                             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Error Handling \u0026 Edge Cases\n\n* **Invalid Tracking Code:** If a user searches for a code that does not exist or has a typo (e.g., `TICK-0000`), Endpoint 1 returns a `404 Not Found` response with a message: *\"Ticket not found.\"*\n* **Empty Resolution Notes on Closure:** If a staff member attempts to mark a ticket as `RESOLVED` without entering a note, Endpoint 3 returns a `400 Bad Request` error: *\"Resolution notes are required when closing a ticket.\"*\n* **Database Connection Outage:** If the database becomes temporarily unavailable, endpoints return a safe `500 Internal Server Error` message without leaking raw server paths or credentials.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Checklist for the Assigned Developer\n\n- [ ] Set up the `GET /api/tickets/{tracking_code}` request handler.\n  - [ ] Implement database query joining `tickets` with `departments`.\n  - [ ] Handle 404 response if the tracking code is invalid.\n- [ ] Set up the `GET /api/tickets` request handler.\n  - [ ] Add query parameter parsing for `department_id` and `status`.\n  - [ ] Implement sorting logic to return newest tickets first (`created_at DESC`).\n- [ ] Set up the `PATCH /api/tickets/{ticket_id}/status` request handler.\n  - [ ] Validate that the incoming status is one of: `SUBMITTED`, `IN_PROGRESS`, `RESOLVED`.\n  - [ ] Validate that `resolution_notes` is provided when transitioning to `RESOLVED`.\n  - [ ] Automatically update `updated_at` and `resolved_at` timestamps in the database.\n- [ ] Test all three endpoints using an API testing client:\n  - Verify reading a ticket by tracking code returns the full data.\n  - Verify filtering by `department_id\u003d2` returns only Plumbing tickets.\n  - Verify moving a ticket to `RESOLVED` correctly saves the resolution note and timestamp.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Handoff Contract (What F3 and F4 Receive)\n\n* **For Module F3 (Public Tracker):** You can call `GET /api/tickets/{tracking_code}` to retrieve real-time status and timestamps for the 3-step progress bar.\n* **For Module F4 (Staff Portal):** You can call `GET /api/tickets` to populate your management table and use `PATCH /api/tickets/{ticket_id}/status` to update ticket statuses directly from table row action buttons.",
