      "text": "# Module F4: Basic Internal Ticket List \u0026 Status Controller — Detailed Blueprint\n\n---\n\n## 1. Module Objective\nTo create the internal staff management interface hosted at the `/admin` route. \n\nThis module provides campus maintenance coordinators and technicians with a centralized dashboard to view all incoming complaints, filter tickets by department or status, inspect complaint details, and update ticket progress (`Submitted` ➔ `In Progress` ➔ `Resolved`) using the **Status Management API (Module B3)**.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Visual Layout \u0026 Screen Architecture\n\nThe staff portal is hosted inside the global shell from **Module F1** and features three main visual zones:\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                      STAFF MAINTENANCE DASHBOARD                       │\n│    Manage, assign, and resolve incoming campus maintenance tickets.   │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                        │\n│  SUMMARY COUNTERS                                                      │\n│  ┌──────────────────┐  ┌──────────────────┐  ┌──────────────────┐      │\n│  │ Total Open       │  │ In Progress      │  │ Resolved Today   │      │\n│  │     14           │  │      6           │  │     22           │      │\n│  └──────────────────┘  └──────────────────┘  └──────────────────┘      │\n│                                                                        │\n│  FILTERS \u0026 CONTROLS                                                    │\n│  Department: [ All Departments ▼ ]    Status: [ All ] [ Submitted ] [ In Progress ] [ Resolved ]\n│                                                                        │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  TICKET DIRECTORY                                                      │\n│                                                                        │\n│  Code       Title \u0026 Location           Department    Status      Date  │  Actions\n│  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  │  ────────────\n│  TICK-8492  Water leak in 2nd floor    [Plumbing]   [Submitted] 10:30A │  [▶ Start] [✓ Resolve]\n│             Hostel Block C, Room 204                                   │\n│                                                                        │\n│  TICK-7120  Flickering light in Lab 3  [Electrical] [In Progress]09:15A│  [✓ Resolve]\n│             Science Block, 1st Floor                                   │\n│                                                                        │\n│  TICK-6019  Broken door lock           [Civil]      [Resolved]  Yesterday│ [View Details]\n│             Main Library, Reading Room                                 │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Summary Metric Cards \u0026 Filter Controls\n\n### 3.1 Quick Summary Metric Bar\nDisplayed prominently at the top of the dashboard to give staff an instant snapshot:\n* **Total Open:** Count of all tickets currently in `SUBMITTED` state.\n* **In Progress:** Count of all tickets currently in `IN_PROGRESS` state.\n* **Resolved:** Count of all tickets marked `RESOLVED`.\n\n---\n\n### 3.2 Filter Controls\nStaff can narrow down the ticket directory using two real-time filter controls without reloading the page:\n1. **Department Dropdown Filter:**\n   * Options: *All Departments*, *Electrical*, *Plumbing*, *Sanitation*, *Civil Maintenance*, *IT Support*, *General Administration*.\n2. **Status Toggle Pills:**\n   * Clickable filter pills: `All`, `Submitted`, `In Progress`, `Resolved`.\n   * Selecting a pill immediately updates the table to display only matching tickets.\n\n---\n\n## 4. The Ticket Table \u0026 Interactive Actions\n\nThe main section displays a structured data table where each row represents an active complaint.\n\n### 4.1 Table Columns\n1. **Reference Code:** Displays the bold tracking code (e.g., `TICK-8492`).\n2. **Title \u0026 Location:** Displays the complaint summary in bold with the specific campus location directly underneath in muted text.\n3. **Department:** Renders the assigned department badge.\n4. **Status:** Renders the color-coded status badge (`SUBMITTED` \u003d Amber, `IN_PROGRESS` \u003d Blue, `RESOLVED` \u003d Green).\n5. **Submitted Date:** Human-readable submission time (e.g., *\"Today, 10:30 AM\"* or *\"Oct 24, 2026\"*).\n6. **Action Controls:** Context-aware action buttons depending on the current status of the row.\n\n---\n\n### 4.2 Row Action Logic \u0026 State Transitions\n\nThe action buttons dynamically change based on where the ticket is in its lifecycle:\n\n```\n[Row Status: SUBMITTED]   ──► Shows: [ ▶ Start Work ] Button\n                                        │\n                                        ▼ (Clicking calls API to move to IN_PROGRESS)\n[Row Status: IN_PROGRESS] ──► Shows: [ ✓ Mark Resolved ] Button\n                                        │\n                                        ▼ (Clicking opens Resolution Modal)\n[Row Status: RESOLVED]    ──► Shows: [ 👁 View Details ] Button (Read-only review)\n```\n\n1. **Action 1: *\"Start Work\"*:**\n   * Available when status is `SUBMITTED`.\n   * Clicking immediately sends a request to **Module B3** to transition the ticket to `IN_PROGRESS`.\n   * The status pill on the row instantly updates to Blue.\n2. **Action 2: *\"Mark Resolved\"*:**\n   * Available when status is `IN_PROGRESS` or `SUBMITTED`.\n   * Clicking opens the **Resolution Notes Modal** (see Section 5).\n3. **Action 3: *\"View Details\"*:**\n   * Available for `RESOLVED` tickets to inspect the full description and the recorded staff fix notes.\n\n---\n\n## 5. The Resolution Notes Modal\n\nTo maintain operational accountability, staff cannot mark a ticket as resolved without documenting what was fixed.\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    RESOLVE TICKET: TICK-8492                │\n│    Provide details of the fix before closing this ticket.   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                             │\n│  Resolution Notes *                                         │\n│  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │\n│  │ e.g., Replaced damaged washer and tightened pipe      │  │\n│  │ joints under the sink. Checked for further leaks.     │  │\n│  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │\n│  (Mandatory: Explain what maintenance actions were taken)   │\n│                                                             │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────┐     ┌───────────────────────┐  │\n│  │ [ Cancel ]              │     │ [ Confirm \u0026 Resolve ] │  │\n│  └─────────────────────────┘     └───────────────────────┘  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### 5.1 Modal Behavior:\n* **Validation:** The *\"Confirm \u0026 Resolve\"* button remains disabled until the staff member enters at least 5 characters in the resolution notes box.\n* **Submission:** When clicked, sends the `PATCH` request to **Module B3** containing the new status `RESOLVED` and the typed `resolution_notes`.\n* **Instant UI Refresh:** Upon success, the modal closes, a green toast notification confirms *\"Ticket marked as resolved\"*, and the table row updates immediately.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Implementation Checklist for the Assigned Developer\n\n- [ ] Place the admin component inside the `/admin` route established in Module F1.\n- [ ] Wire up `GET /api/tickets` to fetch the complete ticket list on page load.\n- [ ] Build the **Summary Metric Bar** calculating counts for Open, In Progress, and Resolved tickets.\n- [ ] Build the **Department Dropdown** and **Status Filter Pills** to dynamically filter the table array in state.\n- [ ] Build the **Ticket Data Table** using the shared `Card`, `Button`, and `Status Badge` primitives from F1.\n- [ ] Implement the 1-click **\"Start Work\"** button action triggering `PATCH /api/tickets/{id}/status` with `IN_PROGRESS`.\n- [ ] Build the **Resolution Notes Modal**:\n  - [ ] Enforce non-empty notes validation.\n  - [ ] Wire up the *\"Confirm \u0026 Resolve\"* button to submit status `RESOLVED` with the note text.\n  - [ ] Handle modal open, close, and loading states.\n- [ ] Build an **Empty State** card displaying *\"No tickets found matching the selected filters\"* when a search yields zero results.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Handoff Contract (Integration Verification)\n\n* **With Module B3 (Backend API):** Module F4 consumes `GET /api/tickets` to render the table and sends updates via `PATCH /api/tickets/{ticket_id}/status`.\n* **With Module F3 (Public Tracker):** When staff resolves a ticket in F4, any user refreshing their tracking screen in F3 will immediately see the progress bar turn green and read the newly entered resolution notes.",
