      "text": "# Module I1: End-to-End Wiring \u0026 System Verification — Detailed Blueprint\n\n---\n\n## 1. Module Objective\nTo connect all independent frontend and backend modules into a unified, functioning application and execute rigorous verification tests. \n\nCompleting this module ensures that **Version 1.0** works as a reliable, closed-loop digital complaint system before adding AI intelligence in Version 2.0.\n\n---\n\n## 2. End-to-End System Connection Map\n\n```\n┌───────────────────────────┐                    ┌───────────────────────────┐\n│     FRONTEND SCREENS      │                    │     BACKEND SERVICES      │\n├───────────────────────────┤                    ├───────────────────────────┤\n│ Module F2:                │  POST /tickets     │ Module B2:                │\n│ Public Submission Form    ├───────────────────►│ Ingestion \u0026 Keyword Rules │\n│                           │◄───────────────────┤                           │\n│                           │  Returns Code      │                           │\n├───────────────────────────┤                    ├───────────────────────────┤\n│ Module F3:                │  GET /tickets/{id} │ Module B3:                │\n│ Public Status Tracker     ├───────────────────►│ Lookup Engine             │\n│                           │◄───────────────────┤                           │\n│                           │  Returns Progress  │                           │\n├───────────────────────────┤                    ├───────────────────────────┤\n│ Module F4:                │  GET /tickets      │ Module B3:                │\n│ Staff Management Portal   │  PATCH /status     │ Directory \u0026 Status Engine │\n│                           ├───────────────────►│                           │\n│                           │◄───────────────────┤                           │\n└───────────────────────────┘                    └─────────────┬─────────────┘\n                                                               │\n                                                               ▼\n                                                 ┌───────────────────────────┐\n                                                 │ Module B1:                │\n                                                 │ PostgreSQL Database       │\n                                                 └───────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Step-by-Step Verification Test Scenarios\n\nThe team must execute and pass **5 core verification scenarios** to formally complete Version 1.0:\n\n---\n\n### Scenario 1: The Standard Ingestion Flow (Keyword Routing)\n* **Action:**\n  1. Open the home page (`/`).\n  2. Enter Title: *\"Water leaking from broken pipe in washroom\"*.\n  3. Enter Location: *\"Hostel Block B, 2nd Floor\"*.\n  4. Enter Description: *\"The main pipe under the sink has burst and water is flooding the floor\"*.\n  5. Click **\"Submit Complaint\"**.\n* **Expected Verification Results:**\n  * [ ] Form shows loading spinner and disables inputs.\n  * [ ] Success Modal appears displaying a valid tracking code (e.g., `TICK-1042`).\n  * [ ] Modal confirms the ticket was automatically routed to the **Plumbing** department.\n  * [ ] Clicking *\"Copy Code\"* copies the code to the clipboard and shows visual confirmation.\n\n---\n\n### Scenario 2: Unmapped Complaint (Fallback Routing)\n* **Action:**\n  1. Submit a complaint with ambiguous text containing zero maintenance keywords:\n     * Title: *\"Strange rattling sound in hallway\"*.\n     * Description: *\"There is a weird noise coming from the corner every few minutes\"*.\n     * Location: *\"Admin Block, Room 10\"*.\n  2. Click **\"Submit Complaint\"**.\n* **Expected Verification Results:**\n  * [ ] Ticket is successfully created without crashing.\n  * [ ] System defaults the assigned department to **General Administration (ID: 6)**.\n\n---\n\n### Scenario 3: Public Status Tracking \u0026 Stepper Inspection\n* **Action:**\n  1. In the Success Modal from Scenario 1, click **\"Track This Complaint\"**.\n  2. System redirects to `/track?code\u003dTICK-1042`.\n* **Expected Verification Results:**\n  * [ ] Search input is automatically filled with `TICK-1042` and fires search instantly.\n  * [ ] Progress bar displays **Step 1 (Submitted)** as active and highlighted.\n  * [ ] Steps 2 (`In Progress`) and 3 (`Resolved`) are displayed as pending gray circles.\n  * [ ] Details card displays correct Title, Location, Plumbing badge, and creation timestamp.\n\n---\n\n### Scenario 4: Staff Work Progression\n* **Action:**\n  1. Open the staff portal (`/admin`) in a separate browser window.\n  2. Locate ticket `TICK-1042` in the table.\n  3. Click **\"Start Work\"**.\n* **Expected Verification Results:**\n  * [ ] Row status badge instantly updates from Amber (`SUBMITTED`) to Blue (`IN_PROGRESS`).\n  * [ ] Return to the user tracking screen (`/track`) and click **\"Refresh Status\"**.\n  * [ ] User progress bar now shows **Step 1 as Complete (Green ✓)** and **Step 2 (In Progress) as Active**.\n\n---\n\n### Scenario 5: Ticket Resolution \u0026 Customer Feedback Loop\n* **Action:**\n  1. In the staff portal (`/admin`), click **\"Mark Resolved\"** on ticket `TICK-1042`.\n  2. Resolution Modal opens.\n  3. Attempt to click \"Confirm \u0026 Resolve\" with an empty note (verify it is blocked).\n  4. Type Resolution Note: *\"Replaced the burst section of pipe and tested water flow. Issue resolved.\"*\n  5. Click **\"Confirm \u0026 Resolve\"**.\n* **Expected Verification Results:**\n  * [ ] Staff table marks ticket status as Green (`RESOLVED`).\n  * [ ] Summary counter at top of admin page increments *\"Resolved Today\"*.\n  * [ ] Return to user tracking screen (`/track`) and click **\"Refresh Status\"**.\n  * [ ] User progress bar displays all 3 steps as **Complete (Green ✓)**.\n  * [ ] The Resolution Notes box appears below the description showing the staff fix details.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Edge Case \u0026 Failure Mode Verification\n\n* [ ] **Invalid Tracking Code:** Search for `TICK-9999` on `/track` ➔ Verifies clean red error card: *\"No complaint found matching code\"*.\n* [ ] **Backend Server Offline:** Stop the backend server and attempt to submit a form on `/` ➔ Verifies red banner appears without losing the user\u0027s typed text.\n* [ ] **Empty Form Submission:** Attempt to submit empty fields on `/` ➔ Verifies client-side validation highlights invalid fields in red before making a network call.\n* [ ] **Department Filtering:** In `/admin`, select *\"Electrical\"* from dropdown ➔ Verifies table only shows electrical tickets.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Version 1.0 Sign-Off Checklist\n\nBefore proceeding to Version 2.0 development, verify all items are completed:\n\n- [x] **Module B1:** Relational Database deployed with pre-seeded departments.\n- [x] **Module F1:** Global Shell, Router, and theme primitives active.\n- [x] **Module B2:** Ingestion API with keyword routing and tracking code generator active.\n- [x] **Module F2:** Submission form with validation and success modal active.\n- [x] **Module B3:** Lookup and status mutation API endpoints active.\n- [x] **Module F3:** Tracking screen with 3-stage progress bar active.\n- [x] **Module F4:** Staff directory with filters and resolution modal active.\n- [x] **Module I1:** All 5 end-to-end test scenarios passed without manual database edits.\n\n---\n\n### **Version 1.0 is officially complete.**\n*The foundation is fully operational. We can now proceed to **Version 2.0 (AI Ingestion \u0026 Smart Categorization)** to replace the basic keyword rules with AI text analysis and deterministic priority ratings.*",
