      "text": "# Version 1.0: Implementation, Git Workflow \u0026 Testing Guide\n\n---\n\n## 1. Team Git \u0026 Branching Strategy\n\nTo prevent team members from overwriting each other\u0027s work or breaking the main project, the team follows a standard **Feature Branch Workflow**:\n\n```\n                  ┌── feature/b1-database ───────► (Merge to develop) ──┐\n                  ├── feature/f1-layout-shell ───► (Merge to develop) ──┤\n                  ├── feature/b2-ingestion-api ──► (Merge to develop) ──┤\n[ main ] ◄─────── [ develop ] ──────────────────────────────────────────┴──► Release v1.0.0\n (Stable)          (Integration)\n                  ├── feature/b3-status-api ─────► (Merge to develop) ──┐\n                  ├── feature/f2-submit-form ────► (Merge to develop) ──┤\n                  ├── feature/f3-status-tracker ─► (Merge to develop) ──┤\n                  └── feature/f4-admin-portal ───► (Merge to develop) ──┘\n```\n\n### 1.1 Branch Hierarchy \u0026 Rules\n1. **`main` Branch (Protected):**\n   * Contains only stable, fully tested code.\n   * **Rule:** Nobody commits directly to `main`. Code is merged into `main` only after Version 1.0 passes all integration tests.\n2. **`develop` Branch (Integration Hub):**\n   * The central working branch where completed features are merged and tested together.\n3. **`feature/*` Branches (Individual Workspaces):**\n   * Every team member creates an isolated branch for their assigned module.\n   * Naming convention:\n     * `feature/b1-database` (Member 1)\n     * `feature/f1-layout` (Member 3)\n     * `feature/b2-ingestion` (Member 1)\n     * `feature/b3-status-api` (Member 2)\n     * `feature/f2-submission-form` (Member 3)\n     * `feature/f3-tracking-screen` (Member 3)\n     * `feature/f4-admin-portal` (Member 4)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Step-by-Step Daily Git Workflow\n\nEvery team member follows this 5-step cycle when working on their assigned module:\n\n```\n[1. Pull Latest develop] ──► [2. Create Feature Branch] ──► [3. Build \u0026 Test Locally]\n                                                                     │\n[5. Pull Request \u0026 Merge] ◄── [4. Push Branch to GitHub] ◄───────────┘\n```\n\n### Step 1: Start from the Latest Code\nBefore starting work each day, update your local repository with changes made by your teammates:\n```bash\ngit checkout develop\ngit pull origin develop\n```\n\n### Step 2: Create Your Isolated Feature Branch\nCreate and switch to your specific module branch:\n```bash\ngit checkout -b feature/f2-submission-form\n```\n\n### Step 3: Implement \u0026 Test Locally\nWork exclusively inside the files assigned to your module (as defined in the File Structure Document). Test your components or endpoints locally.\n\n### Step 4: Commit and Push Changes\nCommit your work with clear, descriptive messages:\n```bash\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"feat(F2): build complaint submission form with validation\"\ngit push origin feature/f2-submission-form\n```\n\n### Step 5: Open a Pull Request (PR) \u0026 Peer Review\n1. Go to GitHub and open a **Pull Request** from your feature branch into `develop`.\n2. At least one teammate must review your code to verify it meets module specifications before clicking **Merge**.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Local Implementation \u0026 Testing Guide (Module-by-Module)\n\nHow each team member builds and verifies their module in isolation before merging:\n\n---\n\n### Track A: Backend Implementation \u0026 Testing (Members 1 \u0026 2)\n\n#### Phase 1: Database Setup (Module B1)\n* **Action:**\n  1. Configure your local database instance.\n  2. Define the Department and Ticket entity models in `app/models/`.\n  3. Run the seed script `app/db/seed_data.py` to insert the 6 default departments.\n* **How to Test Locally:**\n  * Open your database management tool (or command line) and run test queries.\n  * Verify that `departments` contains exactly 6 rows (Electrical, Plumbing, Sanitation, Civil, IT, General Admin).\n  * Verify that manually inserting a ticket with an invalid department ID fails with a foreign key error.\n\n---\n\n#### Phase 2: Ingestion \u0026 Keyword Engine (Module B2)\n* **Action:**\n  1. Define the input/output models in `app/schemas/ticket.py`.\n  2. Implement keyword scanning rules in `app/services/keyword_router.py`.\n  3. Implement code generator in `app/services/code_generator.py`.\n  4. Build the `POST /api/v1/tickets` endpoint in `app/api/v1/endpoints/tickets.py`.\n* **How to Test Locally (Using API Client / Swagger UI):**\n  * **Test 1 (Keyword Match):** Send a POST request with Title *\"Broken bathroom tap leaking\"* ➔ Verify response returns `assigned_department: \"Plumbing\"` and a `TICK-XXXX` code.\n  * **Test 2 (Fallback Match):** Send a POST request with Title *\"Random noise in hallway\"* ➔ Verify response returns `assigned_department: \"General Administration\"`.\n  * **Test 3 (Validation Rejection):** Send a POST request with an empty Title ➔ Verify response returns a `422/400 Bad Request` validation error.\n\n---\n\n#### Phase 3: Status \u0026 Lookup Engine (Module B3)\n* **Action:**\n  1. Implement `GET /api/v1/tickets/{tracking_code}` in `app/services/ticket_service.py`.\n  2. Implement `GET /api/v1/tickets` with department and status filters.\n  3. Implement `PATCH /api/v1/tickets/{ticket_id}/status` enforcing mandatory resolution notes.\n* **How to Test Locally:**\n  * **Test 1 (Lookup):** Send a GET request for a known tracking code (e.g., `TICK-1042`) ➔ Verify it returns full ticket details.\n  * **Test 2 (404 Error):** Send a GET request for `TICK-0000` ➔ Verify it returns a `404 Not Found` response.\n  * **Test 3 (Status Transition):** Send a PATCH request with `status: \"IN_PROGRESS\"` ➔ Verify database status updates and `updated_at` changes.\n  * **Test 4 (Resolution Validation):** Send a PATCH request with `status: \"RESOLVED\"` and an empty note ➔ Verify system rejects the update.\n\n---\n\n### Track B: Frontend Implementation \u0026 Testing (Members 3 \u0026 4)\n\n#### Phase 1: Layout Shell \u0026 Shared Primitives (Module F1)\n* **Action:**\n  1. Set up global styling and color constants in `src/styles/globals.css`.\n  2. Build shared primitives (`Button`, `Input`, `Textarea`, `Card`, `StatusBadge`) in `src/components/ui/`.\n  3. Build `Navbar`, `Footer`, and `Layout` in `src/components/layout/`.\n  4. Configure client-side routing in `src/App.jsx`.\n* **How to Test Locally:**\n  * Start the development server and open `localhost` in your browser.\n  * Click all navigation links (*\"Submit Issue\"*, *\"Track Status\"*, *\"Staff Portal\"*).\n  * Verify that active navigation links highlight properly and the layout does not flicker between pages.\n\n---\n\n#### Phase 2: Submission Form (Module F2)\n* **Action:**\n  1. Build `ComplaintForm.jsx` in `src/components/forms/`.\n  2. Build `SuccessModal.jsx` with copy-to-clipboard functionality.\n* **How to Test Locally:**\n  * Leave all fields blank and click \"Submit\" ➔ Verify red validation error messages appear under inputs.\n  * Type in Title, Location, and Description ➔ Verify character counter updates in real time.\n  * Connect to backend `POST /api/v1/tickets` and submit ➔ Verify the Success Modal opens displaying the generated tracking code.\n\n---\n\n#### Phase 3: Status Tracking Screen (Module F3)\n* **Action:**\n  1. Build `SearchBar.jsx`, `ProgressBar.jsx`, and `DetailsCard.jsx` in `src/components/tracker/`.\n  2. Implement URL query parameter detection (`?code\u003dXXXX`).\n* **How to Test Locally:**\n  * Search for a valid code (e.g., `TICK-1042`) ➔ Verify the 3-step progress bar and details card appear.\n  * Search for a fake code (e.g., `TICK-9999`) ➔ Verify clean red \"Ticket Not Found\" alert box appears.\n  * Navigate to `localhost/track?code\u003dTICK-1042` directly in the browser address bar ➔ Verify it automatically performs the lookup on page load.\n\n---\n\n#### Phase 4: Staff Portal (Module F4)\n* **Action:**\n  1. Build `SummaryCards.jsx`, `FilterBar.jsx`, `TicketTable.jsx`, and `ResolveModal.jsx` in `src/components/admin/`.\n* **How to Test Locally:**\n  * Verify metric cards display correct counts for Open, In Progress, and Resolved.\n  * Change the Department dropdown filter ➔ Verify table rows filter instantly.\n  * Click *\"Start Work\"* on a row ➔ Verify row badge turns Blue (`IN_PROGRESS`).\n  * Click *\"Mark Resolved\"* ➔ Verify modal opens, enter fix notes, submit, and verify row badge turns Green (`RESOLVED`).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Full Integration \u0026 Release Sequence (Module I1)\n\nOnce all feature branches have passed individual checks and are merged into `develop`:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│             VERSION 1.0 INTEGRATION TEST SPRINT             │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. Start clean local database instance                      │\n│ 2. Run backend server (`backend/app/main.py`)               │\n│ 3. Run frontend development server (`frontend/`)            │\n│ 4. Execute the 5 End-to-End Test Scenarios                  │\n│    ├── Scenario 1: Submit complaint with keywords           │\n│    ├── Scenario 2: Submit unmapped fallback complaint       │\n│    ├── Scenario 3: Inspect tracking screen \u0026 stepper        │\n│    ├── Scenario 4: Update status to \u0027In Progress\u0027 in Admin  │\n│    └── Scenario 5: Resolve ticket with mandatory fix note   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 5. If all scenarios pass:                                   │\n│    Create Pull Request: `develop` ──► `main`                │\n│ 6. Tag release in Git: `git tag v1.0.0`                     │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Team Troubleshooting \u0026 Best Practices\n\n1. **Handling Merge Conflicts:**\n   * If two team members edit the same file, Git will pause the merge.\n   * Open the file, discuss with your teammate which version is correct, keep the intended code, and commit the resolved file.\n2. **Never Commit Secrets:**\n   * Never commit `.env` files containing real database passwords or API keys to GitHub. Always commit `.env.example` templates instead.\n3. **Mocking Backend during Frontend Dev:**\n   * If the frontend team finishes a UI screen before the backend endpoint is ready, use temporary hardcoded mock data in `src/services/api.js` so frontend work is never blocked. Once the backend endpoint is merged, swap the mock call for the real API call.",
