      "text": "# Module F1: Detailed File-by-File Assignment \u0026 Specifications\n\n---\n\n## 1. Team Role Allocation for Module F1\n\nModule F1 can be divided cleanly between **two frontend developers** working in parallel on the `feature/f1-layout-shell` branch (or by one developer in two distinct stages):\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        FRONTEND MODULE F1 TEAM                         │\n├────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┤\n│ PERSON A: Layout \u0026 Architecture    │ PERSON B: UI Component Specialist │\n│ • Global Styles \u0026 CSS Tokens       │ • Button Component                │\n│ • Navigation Bar \u0026 Footer          │ • Input \u0026 Textarea Primitives     │\n│ • Layout Wrapper                   │ • Card Container \u0026 Status Badge   │\n│ • Router \u0026 Page Skeletons          │ • Alert Banner Toast              │\n└────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. File-by-File Specifications\n\n---\n\n### [Person A] Area 1: Styling, Layout \u0026 Routing Shell\n\n#### 1. File: `frontend/src/styles/globals.css`\n* **Assigned To:** Person A\n* **Purpose:** Defines the global theme variables, reset rules, and base typography.\n* **What to Implement:**\n  * Define color tokens for the background (neutral dark or clean off-white), card surface background, primary action color (Royal Blue or Bold Amber), and borders.\n  * Define status badge color classes:\n    * `SUBMITTED`: Amber/Yellow background with dark text.\n    * `IN_PROGRESS`: Blue/Purple background with readable text.\n    * `RESOLVED`: Emerald Green background with readable text.\n  * Configure the base font family (clean sans-serif) and global anti-aliasing.\n  * Remove default browser margins and set standard box-sizing.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. File: `frontend/src/components/layout/Navbar.jsx`\n* **Assigned To:** Person A\n* **Purpose:** The fixed top header providing branding and navigation between views.\n* **What to Implement:**\n  * **Branding Container (Left):** Renders the campus grievance portal logo and system title (*\"Campus Care Desk\"*). Clicking the title navigates to `/`.\n  * **Navigation Links (Right):**\n    * Link 1: *\"Submit Issue\"* ➔ routes to `/`\n    * Link 2: *\"Track Status\"* ➔ routes to `/track`\n    * Link 3: *\"Staff Portal\"* ➔ routes to `/admin` (styled distinctly as an outline button).\n  * **Active Route Indicator:** Checks the current active URL path and applies a visual highlight (bold text, distinct color, or bottom indicator bar) to the active link.\n  * **Responsive Mobile Menu:** On narrow screens, collapses links into a simple mobile dropdown or toggle button.\n\n---\n\n#### 3. File: `frontend/src/components/layout/Footer.jsx`\n* **Assigned To:** Person A\n* **Purpose:** The global footer displayed at the bottom of every page.\n* **What to Implement:**\n  * Displays the organization/institution copyright statement.\n  * Displays an emergency assistance reminder (e.g., *\"For immediate electrical or fire emergencies, contact Campus Security\"*).\n  * Shows a subtle green indicator dot reading *\"System Operational\"*.\n\n---\n\n#### 4. File: `frontend/src/components/layout/Layout.jsx`\n* **Assigned To:** Person A\n* **Purpose:** The master container wrapping all page content.\n* **What to Implement:**\n  * Combines `Navbar` at the top, a `Main Content Container` in the middle, and `Footer` at the bottom.\n  * Enforces a maximum content width (e.g., centered container) so wide desktop screens do not stretch forms or tables unnaturally.\n  * Adds uniform vertical padding so page content never touches the edges of the screen.\n\n---\n\n#### 5. Files: Page Placeholders \u0026 Router Configuration\n* **Assigned To:** Person A\n* **Files to Create:**\n  * `frontend/src/pages/SubmitPage.jsx` — Minimal skeleton with a placeholder header: *\"Submit Complaint Page (Ready for Module F2)\"*.\n  * `frontend/src/pages/TrackPage.jsx` — Minimal skeleton with a placeholder header: *\"Track Ticket Page (Ready for Module F3)\"*.\n  * `frontend/src/pages/AdminPage.jsx` — Minimal skeleton with a placeholder header: *\"Staff Portal Page (Ready for Module F4)\"*.\n  * `frontend/src/pages/NotFoundPage.jsx` — 404 screen with a friendly message (*\"Page Not Found\"*) and a *\"Return Home\"* button.\n  * `frontend/src/App.jsx` — Configures the client-side router, registering `/`, `/track`, `/admin`, and the fallback `*` route, all wrapped inside `Layout.jsx`.\n  * `frontend/src/main.jsx` — Mounts `App.jsx` into the root HTML DOM element.\n\n---\n\n### [Person B] Area 2: Reusable UI Primitives (`frontend/src/components/ui/`)\n\nPerson B works inside the `src/components/ui/` folder, building the standard components that will be imported by modules F2, F3, and F4.\n\n---\n\n#### 6. File: `frontend/src/components/ui/Button.jsx`\n* **Assigned To:** Person B\n* **Purpose:** Universal clickable button primitive.\n* **Expected Properties (Props):**\n  * `variant`: Allows `\u0027primary\u0027` (solid accent fill), `\u0027secondary\u0027` (outline/neutral), or `\u0027danger\u0027` (red fill/outline). Defaults to `\u0027primary\u0027`.\n  * `isLoading`: True/false flag. If true, disables clicks and replaces button text with a spinning loader and loading message.\n  * `disabled`: True/false flag to disable the button.\n  * `onClick`: Click event handler function.\n  * `children`: Button label text or icons.\n* **Visual States:** Normal, Hover (slightly brightened), Pressed/Active, and Disabled (dimmed, unclickable).\n\n---\n\n#### 7. File: `frontend/src/components/ui/Input.jsx`\n* **Assigned To:** Person B\n* **Purpose:** Standard single-line text input field.\n* **Expected Properties (Props):**\n  * `label`: Text label displayed directly above the input box (e.g., *\"Complaint Title\"*).\n  * `placeholder`: Subtle example text displayed inside an empty input.\n  * `value` and `onChange`: For state management.\n  * `error`: Optional error text string. If provided, the input border turns red and the error text renders beneath the input in small red text.\n  * `required`: True/false flag adding a red asterisk (`*`) next to the label.\n\n---\n\n#### 8. File: `frontend/src/components/ui/Textarea.jsx`\n* **Assigned To:** Person B\n* **Purpose:** Multi-line text box for detailed descriptions.\n* **Expected Properties (Props):**\n  * `label`: Field label.\n  * `placeholder`: Helpful multi-line placeholder guidance.\n  * `rows`: Default number of visible text lines (default: 4 to 5).\n  * `maxLength`: Maximum allowed characters (e.g., 2000).\n  * `showCount`: True/false flag displaying a live character counter at the bottom right (`Current / 2000`).\n  * `error`: Error message text.\n\n---\n\n#### 9. File: `frontend/src/components/ui/Card.jsx`\n* **Assigned To:** Person B\n* **Purpose:** Clean, rounded container used to frame forms, ticket cards, and metric boxes.\n* **Expected Properties (Props):**\n  * `title`: Optional card header title.\n  * `subtitle`: Optional secondary helper text under the title.\n  * `children`: Content placed inside the card.\n* **Visual Styling:** High-contrast background surface, standardized inner padding, rounded outer corners, and a subtle border.\n\n---\n\n#### 10. File: `frontend/src/components/ui/StatusBadge.jsx`\n* **Assigned To:** Person B\n* **Purpose:** Universal status pill indicator.\n* **Expected Properties (Props):**\n  * `status`: Accepts standard status strings (`SUBMITTED`, `IN_PROGRESS`, `RESOLVED`).\n* **Visual Mapping Logic:**\n  * If `SUBMITTED`: Renders amber/yellow pill with text *\"Submitted\"*.\n  * If `IN_PROGRESS`: Renders blue pill with text *\"In Progress\"*.\n  * If `RESOLVED`: Renders green pill with text *\"Resolved\"*.\n  * Fallback: Renders neutral gray pill for any unknown status.\n\n---\n\n#### 11. File: `frontend/src/components/ui/AlertBanner.jsx`\n* **Assigned To:** Person B\n* **Purpose:** Top notification banner for feedback messages (success notifications or server errors).\n* **Expected Properties (Props):**\n  * `type`: `\u0027success\u0027` (green background), `\u0027error\u0027` (red background), or `\u0027info\u0027` (blue background).\n  * `message`: The notification text to display.\n  * `onClose`: Optional close button trigger.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Parallel Collaboration Workflow (Preventing Conflicts)\n\nTo ensure Person A and Person B can work simultaneously on the same branch without merge conflicts:\n\n```\n[Person A: Working on Shell \u0026 Router]           [Person B: Working on UI Primitives]\n  - Modifies: `globals.css`                       - Creates: `src/components/ui/Button.jsx`\n  - Creates: `src/components/layout/*`            - Creates: `src/components/ui/Input.jsx`\n  - Creates: `src/pages/*` (Placeholders)         - Creates: `src/components/ui/Textarea.jsx`\n  - Creates: `App.jsx` \u0026 `main.jsx`               - Creates: `src/components/ui/Card.jsx`\n                                                  - Creates: `src/components/ui/StatusBadge.jsx`\n                                                  - Creates: `src/components/ui/AlertBanner.jsx`\n```\n\n* **Zero File Collisions:** Person A and Person B do not touch the same files.\n* **Independent Testing:** Person B can create a temporary preview page inside `SubmitPage.jsx` to test all UI components (buttons, badges, inputs) while Person A verifies routing.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Module F1 Completion Checklist\n\nBefore passing the code to developers working on F2, F3, and F4, verify:\n\n- [ ] Navigating between `/`, `/track`, and `/admin` displays the corresponding placeholder page.\n- [ ] Active navbar link highlights correctly depending on which page is open.\n- [ ] Entering a non-existent URL (e.g., `/random-page`) renders the 404 page with a working *\"Return Home\"* button.\n- [ ] `Button` component renders primary, secondary, and loading spinner states correctly.\n- [ ] `Input` and `Textarea` show red error borders and error text when the `error` prop is set.\n- [ ] `Textarea` character counter increments correctly when typing.\n- [ ] `StatusBadge` renders distinct colors for `SUBMITTED`, `IN_PROGRESS`, and `RESOLVED`.\n- [ ] Page layout centers cleanly on both mobile and wide desktop screens.",
